ETL Madness Flow is a zero-dependency XML-driven ETL and data workflow
orchestration suite installed isolated under /opt/flow so its binaries
never overwrite or conflict with base or /usr/local packages:

  - /opt/flow/bin/flow: Core pipeline execution engine, preflight/AST
    validator, HTMX visual builder UI, XSLT/Mermaid diagram generator,
    and repository manager.
  - /opt/flow/bin/crypto_tool: Standalone AES-256-GCM encryption and
    decryption, digital signing (OpenSSL, OpenPGP, PKCS#7/CMS),
    signature verification, and keypair generation utility.
  - /opt/flow/bin/db_importer: SQL Server XML pipeline, options, and
    config repository importer and exporter.

To add /opt/flow/bin, manual pages, and GNU Info pages to your login
shell on OpenBSD, source /etc/profile.d/go-flow.sh from /etc/profile or
~/.profile:

    [ -f /etc/profile.d/go-flow.sh ] && . /etc/profile.d/go-flow.sh
